 ## Overview
-Rational Ray Parameterization for Octree Traversal is a method for tracing rays through an octree using exact rational arithmetic to avoid floating-point precision errors during cell boundary crossing and neighbor finding [S1]. It solves the problem of determining the next cell intersected by a ray when the ray parameters are not integers, which typically occurs when the viewplane is in an arbitrary position in space [S1]. Unlike sibling methods that rely on floating-point comparisons or pre-computed structures, this method guarantees robustness by representing ray parameters as rational numbers (numerator/denominator pairs) and using integer arithmetic for all comparisons and boundary tests [S1]. It builds on [Octree and Tree Traversal](4134-octree-and-tree-traversal.md) by replacing approximate geometric tests with exact arithmetic operations.
